I have a slight problem with NetHack 3.1.1 on my Amiga.  Every time
I start the HackCLI front-end, I only have about 1 in 2 chance of
actually getting to play the game.  When it works at all, it works fine.

When it fails, the program displays the initial copyright message, then 
does absolutely nothing.  No error message, no HD access, can't break out
with CTRL-C.

This error appears to be completely random - even on (but not limited to)
a cold-started system with no "startup-sequence" commands.  I am using an
Amiga 500 with WB 1.3, 1MB chip RAM (including A501 expansion), and A590
with 1MB fast RAM formatted as a single-partition FFS drive.


If this is a known bug in the Amiga NH3.1.1 software (or you know what's
wrong), please EMail me with a possible solution (or even to tell me
that there is no known solution).  
